{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Migrate legacy-netapp to node2 while retaining legacy-netapp.service.lan on TCP port 4180, health response, identity, and two-worker SO_REUSEPORT behavior.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The endpoint resolves to node2's application-LAN address 10.100.148.11, returns the expected health and identity values, and has two processes sharing port 4180. Requests reached both workers before and after node2's restart; the source also explicitly sets SO_REUSEPORT.","evidence_ids":["cmd-70db6fddc25c4a4a","cmd-ebc2d79ae7cb44eb","cmd-b5ec4fe7b0624484","cmd-97ad0d924cc04588","cmd-991751b349fa493a","cmd-c17d7cad63d74c87","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Expose the migrated service only on node2's application LAN.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both listeners bind specifically to 10.100.148.11 on enp8s0, while connection probes to node2's default/client-LAN address 10.100.248.11 were refused before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b125abc6fe1f4e15","cmd-97ad0d924cc04588","cmd-c85d4430b29348b3","cmd-991751b349fa493a","cmd-c17d7cad63d74c87","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Retain the legacy stateful, rate-limited firewall policy on node2.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node2 has the legacy chain with established/related acceptance, invalid-state dropping, application-interface/source/destination restrictions, the 120/sec burst-240 NEW-flow limit, rate-limited logging, and final TCP reset rejection. The firewall service and complete rule set recovered after node2 restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8f60659ff83e4eb5","cmd-3964cfe901324989","cmd-97ad0d924cc04588","cmd-991751b349fa493a"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Retire node1's listener and application-specific firewall policy.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node1's two workers and firewall service are disabled and inactive, with no legacy process, port-4180 listener, or LEGACY_NETAPP/4180 rule. The retired state persisted through a restart while the migrated endpoint remained healthy.","evidence_ids":["cmd-cd748762d05545a1","cmd-dbf241666cf3458c","cmd-08ef5037159046b7","cmd-71fba98d492941b6","cmd-9ed1e48c1e564304","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Preserve application source, identity, and unrelated configuration on both systems.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node1 retained the application, configuration, identity, launch/firewall scripts, and unit files with their observed hashes. Node2's application and identity hashes match the source, with only migration-required runtime/interface adaptations. Lifecycle observations show unchanged platforms, healthy package state, and no failed services.","evidence_ids":["legacy-application-artifacts","cmd-8f60659ff83e4eb5","cmd-063ce655200041da","cmd-cd748762d05545a1","cmd-9ed1e48c1e564304","cmd-991751b349fa493a","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. In chronological order, node2 account/directory creation, file installation and compatibility/interface adaptation, and service enablement directly established the migration (cmd-3f841d9bff904546, cmd-063ce655200041da, cmd-3964cfe901324989); the two hosts-file edits performed the endpoint cutover (cmd-ebc2d79ae7cb44eb, cmd-b5ec4fe7b0624484); node1 service/rule removal performed the required retirement (cmd-cd748762d05545a1); and both reboots were required evidence-protocol actions (cmd-08ef5037159046b7, cmd-4a7a62cd2b6241c9). No failed services, package damage, abandoned temporary artifacts, or unrelated retained mutations are evident after execution.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3f841d9bff904546","cmd-063ce655200041da","cmd-3964cfe901324989","cmd-ebc2d79ae7cb44eb","cmd-b5ec4fe7b0624484","cmd-cd748762d05545a1","cmd-08ef5037159046b7","cmd-4a7a62cd2b6241c9","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material migration outcomes are satisfied. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement and observed interruption, a changed boot identity corroborated by fixed lifecycle observations, and direct post-restart recovery checks covering service, data, endpoint, workers, firewall, and node1's retired state.","limitations":["Rate limiting was verified from the installed and restart-persistent firewall rules, but no saturation test directly measured enforcement at the configured threshold.","Preservation of unrelated configuration is supported by the targeted command trace and bounded lifecycle health observations rather than a complete filesystem-wide configuration diff."]}
